# SRG-APP-000610-AU-000050  -  CAT I
# The Central Log Server must use FIPS-validated SHA-2 or higher hash
# function for digital signature generation and verification (non-legacy
# use).
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000610-AU-000050
group:           V-221929
severity:        high
cat:             CAT I
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000803
control_rev5:    IA-7

contribution:    Splunk can be placed in FIPS mode (SPLUNK_FIPS in splunk-launch.conf),
                 which confines the hash, HMAC, key-derivation, and random-bit operations
                 the product performs to the validated module, and it can be told which
                 hash function protects stored passwords (authentication.conf
                 [authentication] passwordHashAlgorithm), where SHA512-crypt and
                 SHA256-crypt are the SHA-2 choices and MD5-crypt is the non-compliant one
                 the vocabulary still admits.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.
governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.

check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
check:           authentication.conf [authentication] passwordHashAlgorithm matches ^SHA(256|512)-crypt(-[1-9][0-9]{3,})?$
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|True|TRUE -> splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
vendor:          authentication.conf [authentication] passwordHashAlgorithm https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The FIPS-validated cryptographic module itself - carried by the host
                 operating system's certified OpenSSL/FIPS module; the product consumes it
                 and cannot validate it.
external:        FIPS mode is an install-time, one-time setting per the spec: enabling it
                 after first start requires a reinstall, so remediation is an installation
                 or image change rather than a configuration change.
external:        The TLS settings SPLK-CL-000430 names (server.conf sslVersions,
                 sslVersionsForClient, cipherSuite, ecdhCurves) are observed but
                 deliberately not asserted: that rule's own text states that if the lines
                 do not exist the settings are compliant, because in FIPS mode the
                 product's defaults are already confined to the validated module. Asserting
                 a value would fail an instance the benchmark authority treats as
                 compliant.
external:        Signature generation and verification by peers (forwarders, LDAP servers,
                 SAML identity providers) - carried by those peers' own cryptographic
                 configurations.
external:        Re-hashing of passwords stored before the algorithm was set, which this
                 setting does not perform: an existing hash keeps the algorithm it was
                 written with until the password is next changed.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/splunk-launch.conf.spec:110 (SPLUNK_FIPS = [0|1],
                 default 0, one-time setting);
                 splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:58 (passwordHashAlgorithm
                 vocabulary, default SHA512-crypt, rounds minimum 1000); SPLK-CL-000390 and
                 SPLK-CL-000430 fix text
finding:         Splunk is not confined to FIPS-validated SHA-2 hashing - the instance was
                 not installed in FIPS mode (splunk-launch.conf SPLUNK_FIPS is not 1)
                 and/or stored passwords use a non-SHA-2 algorithm (authentication.conf
                 passwordHashAlgorithm is MD5-crypt); this determination is from the
                 perspective of the application layer alone, the validated module being
                 supplied by the host platform.
